WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.630
Without source control, a Power Platform app lives inside its development environment.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:09.250
The environment itself is the only source of truth.

00:00:10.125 --> 00:00:12.447
To move it, the maker gathers the app,

00:00:12.457 --> 00:00:16.875
tables and flows into a solution, and exports it as a managed zip file.

00:00:17.709 --> 00:00:20.179
That zip file is the only thing that travels.

00:00:20.669 --> 00:00:23.259
It's imported into test, and then into production.

00:00:24.248 --> 00:00:29.118
The import might be done by hand, by a custom script, or by Power Platform Pipelines.

00:00:29.968 --> 00:00:32.478
Either way, they all carry the same zip forward.

00:00:33.368 --> 00:00:34.678
Managed means locked.

00:00:35.268 --> 00:00:38.866
Test and prod can't be edited, so every fix goes back to dev,

00:00:38.876 --> 00:00:41.478
gets exported again, and moves up the line.

00:00:42.339 --> 00:00:43.509
But notice what's missing.

00:00:44.039 --> 00:00:45.909
The zip is a snapshot, not a history.

00:00:46.399 --> 00:00:48.629
If dev breaks, there's nothing to go back to.

00:00:48.699 --> 00:00:50.089
That's the gap Git fills.
